Approach: Add behavioral cleanup tests in tests/dispatch-workspace-cleanup.test.ts (and tests/dispatch-workspace-registry.test.ts for the partial-provisioning classification case).

Plan:
1. Protected-case tests (per AC ac-active-inflight-provisioning-artifact-preserved, ac-protection-applies-to-every-destructive-surface):
   - active task refs preserve worktree + dispatch branch + reviewer snapshot (already covered, supplement);
   - in-flight refs supplied as options.activeTaskRefs (queue-to-spawn race) — covered;
   - registry record with lifecycle_state='provisioning' preserves all surfaces; same for stale/integrating/cleanup_blocked;
   - 'closing' record with active ref preserved from reaping (already covered as 'reap-candidate'); add closing+unresolved integration variant;
   - reviewer snapshot path preserved when its canonical record is non-closed registry record;
   - dispatch branches associated with non-closed registry records preserved during orphan-branch sweep;
   - root-directory candidate inside protected worker path preserved.

2. Cleanup-positive (truly orphan): closed records reach reap to closed; truly orphan reviewer-snapshot dir removed; root-dir candidate outside any protected path removed; orphan dispatch branch (no record, no active ref) removed.

3. Ambiguous-state: registry parse failure preserves dispatcher-managed artifacts under worktree root (already covered, add direct helper-level test for branches+paths); load failure protects branches via short-id mapping.

4. Behavioral guardrail per surface: through reconcileDispatchWorkspaceArtifacts, exercise each of metadata-less-worktree / reap-candidate / reviewer-snapshot / root-directory / dispatch-branch with both protected and cleanup-eligible outcomes.

5. Regression test: create bootstrap-like nested files (node_modules/<pkg>/bin/script, package.json) under a worker workspace, run reconcileDispatchWorkspaceArtifacts({activeTaskRefs:[taskRef]}) WITHOUT the metadata file and WITHOUT a registry record, assert the nested files and parent workspace dir survive. Mirrors @plan-dispatch-workspace-in-flight-cleanup-protection bootstrap race.

Will assert via filesystem state + git branch presence + diagnostic stream. Tests must be behavioral (no source-scanning).

